==========================================================================================================
  Gibbons-Hawking temperature   T_GH = H_Lambda*hbar/(2*pi*k_B)
  KMS/detailed balance:  F(-w)/F(+w) = exp(hbar omega/k_B T_GH) = exp(2*pi*omega/H_Lambda)
  so the de Sitter response depends on ONE dimensionless variable   x = 2*pi*omega/H_Lambda
  [OK] L1a de Sitter supplies exactly one dimensionless frequency, x = 2 pi omega/H_Lambda. The 2 pi is the forced content of de Sitter thermality (it is the same 2 pi as in Unruh's a/2pi c). NOTHING here references a galaxy, a rotation curve, or the RAR -- which is the whole point of this route

  the framework's kernel variable   w = omega c/a0 = Z*omega/H_Lambda   (a0 = cH_Lambda/Z)
  [OK] L1b and the kernel's variable is w = omega Z/H_Lambda, so identifying it with x fixes Z ALGEBRAICALLY -- one equation, one unknown, no free parameters and no data

